{#
  Parallel-decomposition commands, emitted for every non-MLIP deck.

  Tiled communication breaks pair_deepmd: it derives a bogus ghost count and
  tries to allocate hundreds of GB (host side). Measured 2026-08-11; removing
  `balance` alone does not help, removing tiled does. tiled/RCB exist to spread
  irregular work over many MPI ranks and we run one rank per GPU, so an MLIP
  run loses nothing by falling back to the default brick decomposition.

  Call as `{% call parallel.emit_tiled_comm(mlip_sheet | default(false)) %}{% endcall %}`:
  the block tag lets trim_blocks drop the call line's own newline, so the
  deck is identical to the inline `{% if %}` block these replace. The
  `caller` reference in each body is what lets a call block invoke it.
#}
{% macro emit_tiled_comm(mlip_sheet) %}
{% set _unused = caller is defined %}
{% if not mlip_sheet %}
comm_style      tiled
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{# balance rcb needs comm_style tiled, so it is suppressed for an MLIP too. #}
{% macro emit_balance_rcb(mlip_sheet) %}
{% set _unused = caller is defined %}
{% if not mlip_sheet %}
balance         1.0 rcb
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
